; Exercise 12-csv-to-json (chapter 12).
;
; (csv-to-json text) reads a CSV text whose first record names the
; columns, and returns a result with the JSON text of an array with one
; object per record after the first, from each column name to its field:
;
;   (csv-to-json "name,score\nAda,91\n")
;   is (:ok "[{\"name\": \"Ada\", \"score\": \"91\"}]")
;
; Fields stay Strings. The failures:
;   the failure of read-csv as it is, for a text that is not CSV
;   (:error "no header")                       for a text with no record
;   (:error "wrong number of fields" number)   for a record with more or
;                                              fewer fields than the header,
;                                              where number counts the
;                                              records from 1, the header
;                                              being record 1
; Then run: tutorial/check.sh 12-csv-to-json

(import list)     ; map, zip, range
(import map)      ; from-entries
(import json)     ; write-json
(import csv)      ; read-csv
(import result)   ; ok, failure, then, map-results

